# Line endings are decided here, not by each developer's git config.
#
# Without this file, whether a checkout produces CRLF or LF depends on every
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting — and the first person whose setting
# differs commits a diff that rewrites every line of every file.

# Normalize text files to LF inside the repository. Working-tree endings stay
# native, so Windows editors still see CRLF.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must be LF in the working tree too: bash refuses a script with
# CRLF endings ("$'\r': command not found"), including under WSL.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
